WEBVTT

00:00:15.730 --> 00:00:16.990
The "Stone Coffin," huh?

00:00:17.730 --> 00:00:19.990
It certainly is appropriately named.

00:00:23.720 --> 00:00:26.000
Residual thoughts still dwelling in the mechs?

00:00:27.990 --> 00:00:30.500
It feels like they're all around us.

00:00:30.820 --> 00:00:31.910
Let's go.

00:00:31.910 --> 00:00:33.650
Y-Yeah.

00:00:41.860 --> 00:00:43.040
We're here,

00:00:44.190 --> 00:00:45.360
Mark Nicht.

00:02:18.720 --> 00:02:21.240
So this is Kazuki curry?

00:02:21.510 --> 00:02:24.110
Does eating it raise your assimilation ratio?

00:02:24.110 --> 00:02:26.500
Shut up and eat. You're being rude to Makabe.

00:02:28.170 --> 00:02:29.180
Welcome.

00:02:29.180 --> 00:02:30.660
I'm starving—

00:02:30.660 --> 00:02:32.310
Wh-Whoa!

00:02:33.210 --> 00:02:34.910
The Human Army...

00:02:34.910 --> 00:02:35.960
This is great!

00:02:36.180 --> 00:02:37.920
They're eating curry.

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:39.260
Hey, Toumi-senpai...

00:02:39.550 --> 00:02:41.500
What are they doing here?

00:02:43.080 --> 00:02:45.260
They say they came to meet Kazuki-kun.

00:02:45.490 --> 00:02:46.150
Huh? What the heck?

00:02:46.150 --> 00:02:47.170
Toumi?
Huh? What the heck?

00:02:47.170 --> 00:02:48.020
Huh? What the heck?

00:02:48.020 --> 00:02:50.270
She's cute, huh?

00:02:50.270 --> 00:02:52.270
Go talk to her.

00:02:52.270 --> 00:02:53.770
Talk to her yourself, Billy.

00:02:53.770 --> 00:02:55.150
Aw, what's with you?

00:02:55.370 --> 00:02:58.150
She's looking again. You sure
are popular, Kazuki-kun.

00:02:58.540 --> 00:03:00.070
She's never even met me.

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:12.580
Nice to meet you.

00:03:14.800 --> 00:03:16.890
You guys are incredible.

00:03:16.890 --> 00:03:21.320
I can't believe you can keep
fighting as your own unit!

00:03:21.320 --> 00:03:22.220
Y-Yeah.

00:03:22.650 --> 00:03:24.850
But why don't you help anyone?

00:03:28.350 --> 00:03:31.120
With you around, a lot more
people could survive.

00:03:31.120 --> 00:03:32.980
Why won't you fight with us?

00:03:36.640 --> 00:03:37.790
What have

00:03:39.430 --> 00:03:41.320
you people done for us?

00:03:41.740 --> 00:03:45.070
You occupied our island, dropped bombs on it...

00:03:45.440 --> 00:03:48.280
What are you talking about? I think
you have the wrong idea.

00:03:49.500 --> 00:03:51.760
Don't give me that crap!

00:03:52.860 --> 00:03:53.960
Rina-chan...

00:03:56.340 --> 00:03:57.860
Apologize to her, Billy.

00:03:58.870 --> 00:04:00.920
They gave us their power,

00:04:01.720 --> 00:04:04.200
but did we ever help them?

00:04:04.610 --> 00:04:07.430
After being isolated, they've continued to fight.

00:04:07.750 --> 00:04:08.560
Apologize.

00:04:12.170 --> 00:04:13.450
I'm sorry.

00:04:14.710 --> 00:04:15.440
Um...

00:04:15.820 --> 00:04:17.440
What do you mean by "power"?

00:04:19.820 --> 00:04:20.940
The Makabe factor.

00:04:26.220 --> 00:04:28.650
Long ago, Kazuki Makabe

00:04:28.650 --> 00:04:31.430
assisted the Neo United Nations
in developing a new Fafner.

00:04:32.190 --> 00:04:35.960
At that time, a miracle drug was
created using his genes.

00:04:36.310 --> 00:04:40.920
It enables people who lack the necessary
qualities able to pilot Fafners.

00:04:41.180 --> 00:04:43.250
I'm grateful, Makabe.

00:04:43.250 --> 00:04:46.200
You gave me a chance to pilot a Fafner.

00:04:46.510 --> 00:04:47.540
I'm going on a delivery.

00:04:57.940 --> 00:04:59.200
Maya Toumi.

00:04:59.680 --> 00:05:00.270
Yes?

00:05:00.270 --> 00:05:02.050
I see... You're—

00:05:02.050 --> 00:05:03.420
Hey!

00:05:03.420 --> 00:05:04.520
Do you have a boyfriend?

00:05:04.520 --> 00:05:05.510
She doesn't!

00:05:05.510 --> 00:05:06.910
Chill out, Akira.

00:05:06.910 --> 00:05:08.380
She doesn't?

00:05:08.380 --> 00:05:12.030
Be quiet, Billy. I need to talk with her.

00:05:12.030 --> 00:05:13.690
No fair, keeping her to yourself—

00:05:13.690 --> 00:05:14.410
Billy...

00:05:14.720 --> 00:05:16.330
Come here.

00:05:16.840 --> 00:05:18.790
What the heck?

00:05:19.480 --> 00:05:21.470
Ai likes Mitsuhiro—

00:05:25.570 --> 00:05:26.950
I will hit you.

00:05:29.140 --> 00:05:30.930
Billy means no harm.

00:05:31.410 --> 00:05:32.430
Forgive him.

00:05:32.890 --> 00:05:34.430
What did you want to talk about?

00:05:36.340 --> 00:05:37.880
Mitsuhiro Bartland.

00:05:39.180 --> 00:05:41.940
It's the name of a man who
died developing a Fafner.

00:05:42.440 --> 00:05:44.790
Yeah. I know.

00:05:45.660 --> 00:05:49.740
I heard about this island, D Island, from him.

00:05:49.980 --> 00:05:51.060
And about you.

00:05:52.180 --> 00:05:53.240
Me?

00:05:53.590 --> 00:05:57.000
Bartland was my father.

00:05:57.800 --> 00:06:00.060
That means you and I are...

00:06:00.650 --> 00:06:01.500
Siblings?

00:06:04.790 --> 00:06:06.100
That's right.

00:06:09.430 --> 00:06:11.510
No signs that it's booted up.

00:06:12.970 --> 00:06:15.080
Yet it got into the system.

00:06:15.910 --> 00:06:16.870
It's a monster.

00:06:17.500 --> 00:06:20.400
Shouldn't it stay silent, as long
as the core isn't removed?

00:06:20.400 --> 00:06:24.050
Our current technology can't extract
the core from this one.

00:06:24.050 --> 00:06:27.430
Like Sein, it assimilates our equipment.

00:06:27.430 --> 00:06:30.030
All we can do is seal it away so
the enemy doesn't take it.

00:06:30.660 --> 00:06:32.210
I will bury it.

00:06:32.770 --> 00:06:34.540
I'll stake my very existence on it.

00:06:36.510 --> 00:06:37.850
You aren't surprised?

00:06:38.920 --> 00:06:41.790
It's so sudden. It hasn't hit me yet.

00:06:42.420 --> 00:06:45.070
I'm eighteen years old. You?

00:06:45.070 --> 00:06:45.800
Nineteen.

00:06:46.600 --> 00:06:48.100
So I'm the younger...

00:06:49.620 --> 00:06:51.220
Was our father kind?

00:06:51.720 --> 00:06:53.300
At times, he was.

00:06:53.720 --> 00:06:55.690
And at many other times, he wasn't.

00:06:57.190 --> 00:07:01.750
I often felt as if I were being
forced to act as his lab rat.

00:07:04.690 --> 00:07:06.230
What was your mom like?

00:07:06.760 --> 00:07:08.570
She was kind.

00:07:08.570 --> 00:07:12.240
But when I was young, she was
killed during a battle.

00:07:12.690 --> 00:07:13.530
I see.

00:07:15.370 --> 00:07:18.930
Father's life was nothing more
than revenge on the Festum.

00:07:19.720 --> 00:07:20.750
But not mine.

00:07:21.300 --> 00:07:22.900
I learned about all of you.

00:07:23.700 --> 00:07:24.810
So please...

00:07:25.940 --> 00:07:27.550
Let me meet your family.

00:07:27.550 --> 00:07:28.300
Eh?

00:07:28.300 --> 00:07:30.910
The child of hope that Emery found, Miwa...

00:07:30.910 --> 00:07:34.050
I'm related to her, as well.

00:07:34.760 --> 00:07:38.210
To protect them, I'm not afraid to risk my life.

00:07:39.700 --> 00:07:40.260
See?

00:07:40.260 --> 00:07:41.320
Yeah.

00:07:41.320 --> 00:07:42.280
That's right.

00:07:42.280 --> 00:07:43.310
I thought so!

00:07:43.310 --> 00:07:44.030
And then—

00:07:44.030 --> 00:07:46.690
Then, you two have been talking?

00:07:46.690 --> 00:07:48.440
Yeah, about lots of stuff.

00:07:48.440 --> 00:07:52.630
About food, our families, Tatsumiyajima,
Srinagar, and Mir,

00:07:52.630 --> 00:07:54.600
and about the air here. Right?

00:07:54.600 --> 00:07:55.320
Yeah.

00:07:55.570 --> 00:07:57.920
S-Srinagar?

00:07:57.920 --> 00:08:00.200
You talk about all that at once?

00:08:00.200 --> 00:08:01.210
Yeah!

00:08:01.210 --> 00:08:02.890
O-Oh...

00:08:04.770 --> 00:08:09.430
All the members of my unit possess
the innate qualities of Esperanto.

00:08:09.430 --> 00:08:11.840
That is how they have survived hell itself.

00:08:12.050 --> 00:08:13.840
I believe this island is the same.

00:08:14.680 --> 00:08:17.220
Though none can rival Miwa-kun.

00:08:17.220 --> 00:08:19.450
Emery has said the same.

00:08:19.450 --> 00:08:22.280
She is the world's supreme Esperanto.

00:08:22.280 --> 00:08:24.600
I would like her to meet our Mir.

00:08:24.920 --> 00:08:26.400
Your Mir?

00:08:27.000 --> 00:08:29.850
To us, Mir is a giant tree.

00:08:30.530 --> 00:08:32.830
The Festum are given life by that tree,

00:08:32.830 --> 00:08:35.610
and their life force makes the tree grow.

00:08:35.900 --> 00:08:39.850
A symbiotic relationship between Mir,
a crystalline body of energy,

00:08:39.850 --> 00:08:42.260
and the Festum, silicon life forms...

00:08:42.780 --> 00:08:46.120
We have a general understanding
of it, but it is largely a mystery.

00:08:46.120 --> 00:08:49.000
But we have the means to
learn from experience.

00:08:49.000 --> 00:08:52.010
To make the enemy's power our own...

00:08:52.350 --> 00:08:53.710
Precisely.

00:08:53.710 --> 00:08:57.760
But fighting the Festum with that
power will not bring victory.

00:08:57.760 --> 00:09:02.170
We must converse with Mir and make its
coexistence with humanity a reality.

00:09:02.580 --> 00:09:06.200
Just as the Mir here has transformed into
the atmosphere protecting the island.

00:09:07.380 --> 00:09:09.770
I never thought the Human
Army would tell me that.

00:09:10.210 --> 00:09:12.870
In the Human Army, there is more
than one way of thinking.

00:09:13.390 --> 00:09:16.410
We no longer have the time to
share a single way of thinking.

00:09:16.910 --> 00:09:17.910
What do you mean?

00:09:18.320 --> 00:09:21.170
Our Mir has told us

00:09:21.170 --> 00:09:24.910
of a future in which a new
Mir comes to this planet.

00:09:25.550 --> 00:09:26.620
What?

00:09:34.020 --> 00:09:35.670
What are you doing here?

00:09:37.660 --> 00:09:38.680
Delivery.

00:09:39.300 --> 00:09:41.680
We have named it Altair,

00:09:41.680 --> 00:09:44.350
but attempts to communicate with it have failed.

00:09:44.820 --> 00:09:47.560
Something prevents us from
communicating with it.

00:09:48.040 --> 00:09:50.690
You must have seen this massive enemy, as well.

00:09:51.250 --> 00:09:53.320
That was a Festum?

00:09:53.320 --> 00:09:55.010
An Azazel-type,

00:09:55.010 --> 00:09:59.210
born from a fragment of Mir, and harboring
animosity toward mankind.

00:10:00.150 --> 00:10:01.950
If it calls Altair to itself,

00:10:01.950 --> 00:10:04.710
the human race will fall into further despair.

00:10:05.300 --> 00:10:07.990
We wish to borrow Miwa's power
before that can happen.

00:10:07.990 --> 00:10:09.660
Yeah, that's right!

00:10:11.180 --> 00:10:13.570
And then, guess what?

00:10:17.470 --> 00:10:19.470
"Makabe factor," huh?

00:10:19.760 --> 00:10:20.970
That's typical of the Human Army.

00:10:23.050 --> 00:10:25.350
Are they going to turn out just like me?

00:10:26.040 --> 00:10:27.730
We don't know what sort of factor it is.

00:10:28.340 --> 00:10:29.480
But we know some things.

00:10:30.660 --> 00:10:34.900
At their age, if they've undergone chromosomal
transformation and assimilation,

00:10:35.390 --> 00:10:37.810
they won't survive past their twenties.

00:10:38.680 --> 00:10:40.860
That's the longest they can live.

00:10:41.590 --> 00:10:45.370
And yet, they thanked me...

00:10:45.580 --> 00:10:47.190
It's not your fault.

00:10:47.700 --> 00:10:49.020
If we'd been in that position,

00:10:49.020 --> 00:10:52.040
we'd have fought using a factor
from someone, also.

00:10:54.400 --> 00:10:55.390
I guess so.

00:11:01.300 --> 00:11:02.400
It's grown long.

00:11:03.220 --> 00:11:04.180
Why don't you cut it?

00:11:05.750 --> 00:11:07.540
It's a part of me.

00:11:07.540 --> 00:11:11.550
When I think that it's alive, I can't cut it.

00:11:12.460 --> 00:11:13.270
Oh.

00:11:14.460 --> 00:11:16.170
That's a little irritating.

00:11:16.870 --> 00:11:18.250
You're one to talk.

00:11:20.390 --> 00:11:21.780
You look unhappy.

00:11:22.790 --> 00:11:23.880
Not really.

00:11:25.290 --> 00:11:28.920
You don't mind that you haven't met
the people you fought with?

00:11:28.920 --> 00:11:32.670
I never saw their faces.
We'd have nothing to discuss.

00:11:32.670 --> 00:11:35.370
I have no comrades who mean
more to me than you guys.

00:11:35.370 --> 00:11:36.340
Okay.

00:11:40.770 --> 00:11:42.480
If something's on your mind, you can talk to me.

00:11:43.010 --> 00:11:45.680
Apparently, I have a younger brother now.

00:11:47.710 --> 00:11:50.850
O-Oh, I see! Well, these things happen!

00:11:50.850 --> 00:11:52.390
It's not a bad thing.

00:11:53.240 --> 00:11:53.940
Huh?

00:11:54.910 --> 00:11:58.690
So, who's Toumi-sensei's partner?
Commander Makabe?

00:11:58.690 --> 00:12:00.690
Of course not!

00:12:02.170 --> 00:12:04.110
Are you all right, Toumi-sensei?

00:12:04.110 --> 00:12:05.150
Is it a cold?

00:12:05.150 --> 00:12:06.950
Oh... No, I'm sorry.

00:12:06.950 --> 00:12:12.310
Anyway, Miwa-chan has responded affirmatively
to everything the Human Army has said.

00:12:12.310 --> 00:12:15.460
The lie detector results were
in agreement, as well.

00:12:16.960 --> 00:12:18.210
The Mir they spoke of

00:12:18.680 --> 00:12:21.210
is in Srinagar, in northern India.

00:12:21.460 --> 00:12:23.990
The fact that they won't bring it to the island

00:12:23.990 --> 00:12:28.160
must mean it's either extremely
large or rooted to the ground.

00:12:28.160 --> 00:12:31.980
I'm deeply interested in learning what
this Mir has transformed into.

00:12:32.250 --> 00:12:34.710
We can't approach the island by land.

00:12:34.710 --> 00:12:37.740
There's no way we can send Miwa-chan alone.

00:12:37.740 --> 00:12:40.150
If a Fafner unit is sent to escort her,

00:12:40.150 --> 00:12:42.360
it may lower the island's defenses.

00:12:42.870 --> 00:12:45.140
Four pilots have retired.

00:12:45.140 --> 00:12:47.340
The new candidates have yet
to undergo connection tests,

00:12:47.340 --> 00:12:49.250
and their parents have not been notified.

00:12:50.290 --> 00:12:51.700
And the improved Fafners?

00:12:52.290 --> 00:12:54.390
The third machine is nearly complete,

00:12:54.390 --> 00:12:57.100
but we lack the core to equip it.

00:12:57.100 --> 00:12:59.530
Without a core, it's no different
than conventional weaponry.

00:12:59.530 --> 00:13:01.050
It can't stand against the enemy.

00:13:01.050 --> 00:13:03.840
The eighth machine is currently
equipped with a core,

00:13:03.840 --> 00:13:07.240
but Drei and Acht are being used
for unmanned mech training,

00:13:07.240 --> 00:13:09.290
so only the sixth can be piloted.

00:13:09.290 --> 00:13:10.320
And Solomon?

00:13:10.840 --> 00:13:13.310
Regarding the giant enemy referred
to as the Azazel-type,

00:13:13.720 --> 00:13:15.810
Solomon's responses have been intermittent.

00:13:16.100 --> 00:13:19.310
I believe it's very possible that
it is tracking the island.

00:13:19.760 --> 00:13:22.320
We can't reduce our battle-ready forces.

00:13:22.320 --> 00:13:25.570
Even if we put our trust in them,
the reality is harsh.

00:13:26.100 --> 00:13:28.700
Actually, the general offered a suggestion.

00:13:29.250 --> 00:13:32.200
He says the girl can increase
the island's military strength.

00:13:32.410 --> 00:13:34.200
Increase it? How?

00:13:34.670 --> 00:13:40.570
He wants to let her speak to the
island's core, Minashiro Tsubaki.

00:13:41.470 --> 00:13:42.530
What?

00:13:42.530 --> 00:13:46.230
He wants to make contact with
the island's Mir via the core.

00:13:46.230 --> 00:13:48.970
I can't imagine what he intends to do after that.

00:13:49.220 --> 00:13:50.950
Is it safe?

00:13:50.950 --> 00:13:54.220
Miwa-chan has said she would only talk to her.

00:13:55.140 --> 00:13:58.230
In the morning, we'll have the
girl meet Minashiro Tsubaki.

00:13:58.590 --> 00:14:01.380
Observe all areas. If anything abnormal
happens, we call it off.

00:14:01.380 --> 00:14:02.160
Any objections?

00:14:04.060 --> 00:14:06.010
The hope they speak of...

00:14:06.010 --> 00:14:10.050
Let us pray that it may also be beneficial
to the being we call our core.

00:14:16.040 --> 00:14:17.580
Family, huh?

00:14:17.790 --> 00:14:21.060
My sister hates our dad,

00:14:21.060 --> 00:14:23.090
and I doubt Mom really cares to know.

00:14:25.560 --> 00:14:28.590
On this island, I gained family.

00:14:28.800 --> 00:14:29.590
Yeah.

00:14:30.030 --> 00:14:31.870
I was always alone.

00:14:31.870 --> 00:14:34.600
I had given up on having my own ideas.

00:14:34.890 --> 00:14:39.600
But you, Kazuki, and everyone
on the island changed me.

00:14:40.460 --> 00:14:44.610
If you don't hate him, I think
you should accept him.

00:14:45.560 --> 00:14:47.420
Yeah, you're right.

00:14:48.330 --> 00:14:49.620
Thanks, Canon.

00:14:51.660 --> 00:14:55.120
I wanted to talk to you, too. About Kazuki.

00:14:55.120 --> 00:14:57.770
About him going to see Mark Sein?

00:14:57.770 --> 00:14:59.300
You knew?

00:14:59.300 --> 00:15:01.240
I had a hunch.

00:15:02.210 --> 00:15:05.090
Battle was always the only
place where he belonged.

00:15:05.510 --> 00:15:09.170
But now, Kazuki-kun belongs here.

00:15:09.650 --> 00:15:10.740
He'll be fine.

00:15:12.280 --> 00:15:15.010
You understand Kazuki pretty well.

00:15:15.810 --> 00:15:18.370
No, I don't. That's just what I think.

00:15:18.370 --> 00:15:20.890
Is that why you're trying to protect him?

00:15:21.210 --> 00:15:22.150
Huh?

00:15:22.150 --> 00:15:25.520
Is your working on Takerujima
and piloting the Fafner

00:15:25.850 --> 00:15:27.890
all to protect the place where Kazuki is?

00:15:30.050 --> 00:15:31.100
I don't know.

00:15:32.010 --> 00:15:34.070
Before I knew it, that's just what I was doing.

00:15:41.100 --> 00:15:42.210
Tsubaki-chan?

00:15:43.610 --> 00:15:46.090
I can't believe she grew so rapidly...

00:15:47.170 --> 00:15:49.290
Did she accelerate her own growth?

00:15:49.940 --> 00:15:52.090
A core in the form of a human.

00:15:52.440 --> 00:15:54.520
A fusion of human and Mir?

00:15:54.520 --> 00:15:56.780
I've never seen this in person before.

00:15:56.780 --> 00:15:59.980
She's a very kind, sad girl...

00:15:59.980 --> 00:16:00.930
Wait!

00:16:10.700 --> 00:16:14.390
You've protected everyone
all this time, haven't you?

00:16:16.450 --> 00:16:19.600
Give us your strength.

00:16:23.000 --> 00:16:23.920
Emery!

00:16:25.430 --> 00:16:26.710
She'll be assimilated by the Mir!

00:16:26.930 --> 00:16:28.500
It's dangerous! Get back!

00:16:28.980 --> 00:16:30.150
I see.

00:16:30.900 --> 00:16:34.470
The core before you sacrificed itself, too.

00:16:34.470 --> 00:16:37.260
No! Don't go away!

00:16:37.260 --> 00:16:38.760
Stop her right now!

00:16:39.320 --> 00:16:43.270
One cannot converse with Mir without
being prepared to pay the price.

00:16:43.600 --> 00:16:45.020
What?

00:16:47.010 --> 00:16:50.490
If it comes to it, I will be the one to disappear.

00:16:52.720 --> 00:16:55.740
There was a time when I sacrificed many thousands,

00:16:55.990 --> 00:16:59.490
but I'm not so foolish as to lose the
key to humanity's salvation.

00:17:00.460 --> 00:17:03.120
Hundreds of Esperantos are waiting for you.

00:17:03.830 --> 00:17:07.250
They would all gladly act as
shields for you and Emery.

00:17:14.760 --> 00:17:16.760
The island's Mir is resonating.

00:17:25.450 --> 00:17:26.690
Thank you...

00:17:30.260 --> 00:17:31.220
Emery!

00:17:36.290 --> 00:17:37.950
She answered me.

00:17:41.330 --> 00:17:42.800
Response from Solomon.

00:17:42.800 --> 00:17:43.590
It's in the ship!

00:17:43.590 --> 00:17:44.200
Where?

00:17:44.420 --> 00:17:46.240
Abnormality found in the keel block.

00:17:46.240 --> 00:17:48.960
Something just appeared...
From the Well of Urd?

00:17:57.840 --> 00:17:58.840
What is that?

00:17:59.920 --> 00:18:02.230
Solomon has identified it as the island's Mir.

00:18:02.760 --> 00:18:05.160
Something with the same code
as a Fafner has appeared.

00:18:05.160 --> 00:18:06.270
More are appearing.

00:18:06.270 --> 00:18:07.410
Get it on the monitor.

00:18:10.760 --> 00:18:13.270
Is this even possible?

00:18:13.650 --> 00:18:16.280
A core just rose from the Well of Urd?

00:18:16.800 --> 00:18:18.140
Now we can fight.

00:18:18.650 --> 00:18:22.850
Now lots more people can fight for a long time.

00:18:22.850 --> 00:18:23.790
Emery?

00:18:23.790 --> 00:18:27.390
No. That isn't what Tsubaki-chan wants.

00:18:27.390 --> 00:18:28.290
It can't be...

00:18:34.520 --> 00:18:37.090
Is this the will of the island?

00:18:40.500 --> 00:18:44.240
I am also being kept alive by the Festum.

00:18:44.240 --> 00:18:45.690
Just like you.

00:18:49.330 --> 00:18:51.270
Look at all the cores!

00:18:51.720 --> 00:18:56.050
Not only can we finish the remodels, we can
rebuild the unnumbered mechs, too.

00:18:56.690 --> 00:19:00.200
Yes, assuming they're all
compatible with the mechs.

00:19:00.200 --> 00:19:04.850
If they are, deploying the unmanned mechs
in battle won't be a mere dream.

00:19:07.900 --> 00:19:08.580
EC breakout! EC breakout!

00:19:08.580 --> 00:19:10.120
Cut off the arm!

00:19:13.840 --> 00:19:15.840
Why did that happen?

00:19:16.360 --> 00:19:18.750
The Well of Urd is supposed to be

00:19:18.750 --> 00:19:20.840
the liquid computer that functions
as Solomon's brain, right?

00:19:21.590 --> 00:19:24.490
It's also where Minashiro Tsubaki was born.

00:19:24.490 --> 00:19:26.350
The island's core?

00:19:26.580 --> 00:19:29.970
Long ago, the Mir assimilated a researcher.

00:19:30.680 --> 00:19:32.680
Her name was Minashiro Saya.

00:19:32.680 --> 00:19:35.140
She was with child.

00:20:11.910 --> 00:20:14.150
The Mir transformed a human...

00:20:14.370 --> 00:20:16.840
After that, the thing that was once Saya

00:20:16.840 --> 00:20:19.850
upgraded to a liquid computer
for analytical functions...

00:20:20.740 --> 00:20:23.660
To find out whether her will remained in it or not.

00:20:23.910 --> 00:20:26.320
And as a result, that Well became

00:20:26.320 --> 00:20:29.910
our only means of reading the enemy.

00:20:29.910 --> 00:20:33.740
Do you believe Minashiro Saya is still here?

00:20:33.740 --> 00:20:36.540
Her human consciousness no longer exists.

00:20:36.540 --> 00:20:40.550
But it is a fact that, because of her,
the Mir transformed.

00:20:41.170 --> 00:20:45.300
That transformation may still be ongoing.

00:20:46.680 --> 00:20:50.770
All the cores that appeared are compatible
with the Fafner system.

00:20:52.840 --> 00:20:55.710
This certainly will double our defenses.

00:20:55.710 --> 00:20:58.770
What's curious is that the mechs'
potential has increased.

00:20:59.260 --> 00:21:01.480
Isn't that a good thing?

00:21:01.740 --> 00:21:04.850
It isn't only in ones equipped with new cores.

00:21:05.350 --> 00:21:09.030
The mechs that were here before
have been affected, as well.

00:21:09.030 --> 00:21:09.740
Affected?

00:21:09.740 --> 00:21:11.500
Not as much as Sein,

00:21:11.500 --> 00:21:15.840
but their core housing blocks are forming
vaporous perpetual-conductive circuits.

00:21:15.840 --> 00:21:19.290
In other words, they're converting
materials in the air into energy.

00:21:19.290 --> 00:21:22.930
Their original power sources
aren't being consumed at all.

00:21:22.930 --> 00:21:25.760
The mechs themselves have
turned into black boxes.

00:21:25.760 --> 00:21:28.900
There's no telling what will happen.

00:21:28.900 --> 00:21:32.270
All three new pilot candidates have
passed their connection tests.

00:21:32.530 --> 00:21:35.250
No change was observed after
they boarded the mechs.

00:21:35.250 --> 00:21:37.020
In fact, when they boarded,

00:21:37.020 --> 00:21:39.970
they showed the same symptoms as
if they'd been given too much of the

00:21:39.970 --> 00:21:41.770
assimilation-phenomenon prevention drug.

00:21:42.030 --> 00:21:44.530
The mechs are protecting the pilots?

00:21:44.530 --> 00:21:46.310
We can't draw any conclusions,

00:21:46.310 --> 00:21:48.920
but from the physical changes
we've observed in the pilots,

00:21:48.920 --> 00:21:50.160
that is very possible.

00:21:50.380 --> 00:21:53.660
I'd love to just believe that this island's core

00:21:53.660 --> 00:21:56.220
has given us a new power, but...

00:21:56.220 --> 00:22:00.770
Until the pilots actually get in the mechs
and fight, there's no way to know.

00:22:00.770 --> 00:22:02.170
These weapons really are bad luck.

00:22:02.730 --> 00:22:06.300
Whether or not we gain an expeditionary
force to send outside the island

00:22:06.300 --> 00:22:08.550
will depend on the new mechs and pilots.

00:22:09.300 --> 00:22:11.780
I officially authorize the three candidates as pilots.

00:22:11.780 --> 00:22:13.710
They will begin the training regimen.

00:22:13.710 --> 00:22:16.560
I will notify their families.

00:22:17.180 --> 00:22:20.250
Let's pray for the health and
success of our new soldiers.

00:22:24.260 --> 00:22:25.240
So, you're here?

00:22:26.490 --> 00:22:30.200
This was the first price paid for that conversation.

00:22:32.350 --> 00:22:37.510
You will soon learn that both conversation
and battle come at a price.

00:22:40.710 --> 00:22:43.210
That is the unchanging question of this world,

00:22:43.730 --> 00:22:48.430
and the answer is our lives themselves.

00:24:22.470 --> 00:24:25.420
<i>Fafner in the Azure: Exodus</i>, episode 4:

00:24:25.420 --> 00:24:26.980
The Successors.
